{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310875,"nonce":"pipxutynBQOpZYcgzQ9s+DXJ/2o=","title":"Native WorkerPool blocker was FIVE stacked bugs, not one. ALL FIVE FIXED — WorkerPool.withForcedNodes(N).parallelRows now runs end-to-end ...","message":"The \"WorkerPool.withForcedNodes hangs\" blocker (old BUG 1c) was **FIVE stacked, distinct bugs**, peeled back one layer at a time. **ALL RESOLVED** — `WorkerPool.withForcedNodes(4).parallelRows(16, (lo,hi,node)-\u003e{...})` now runs end-to-end with correct band sums on native + wasm (WPuse out=6,22,38,54). Branch `wasm-default-inguest-matmul`. All fixes verified regression-free via before/after output A/B (see [[feedback_regression_output_coherence]]); haxe 134-pass, e2e green, concurrency 4/4 native+wasm.\n\n1. **8a95926d — closure-Dynamic typing.** Untyped lambda params (`(a,b,c)-\u003e...`) passed to a function-typed param of a SAME-CLASS STATIC method dropped to Dynamic (`*void` MIR formals) → body unboxed via haxe_unbox_int_ptr while caller passed raw i32 → SIGSEGV. Root: `resolve_callee_formal_param_types` Ident branch only did bare `lookup_symbol` (misses same-class static/instance methods); now falls back to `resolve_class_method_symbol`. Test test_untyped_closure_param_inference.\n2. **4e9a1409 — monomorphizer id-space collision (SYSTEMIC).** Monomorphizer minted instance ids from fixed 10_000; import-merge renumbers each import module by `100_000 + N*10_000` (stride 10_000). A mono instance at local 10_000 in module N → `base(N)+10_000 == base(N+1)` = slot-0 (the `malloc` extern) of the NEXT import module → merge silently overwrote malloc. So `new WorkerPool()`'s alloc CallDirect dispatched into a BalancedTree `get_height__i64_i64`, returned a tree height (small int) as the object ptr → `ldr [0x38]` SIGSEGV. Found via multi-agent merged-MIR analysis (`fn230000 = @get_height__i64_i64`). Fix: seed `next_func_id` above the module's max id in `monomorphize_module`. Test test_stdlib_self_construct.\n3. **67d968e4 — callee-hint exponential compile hang.** The best-effort lambda-arg hint (`resolve_callee_*`) lowers the call RECEIVER; a call-valued receiver re-enters lower_call_expression which resolves hints again — twice per call → O(2^depth), unbounded compile hang on parallelRows. Fix: `suppress_callee_hint` re-entrancy guard.\n4. **bcb304a8 — loop counter from a parameter never advances (THE runtime root).** Loop-phi construction excluded params by REGISTER (`symbol_map.get(sym)==Some(\u0026p.reg)`). `var i = lo` aliases i to lo's register, so the counter was misclassified as the param → no loop phi → `i++` discarded, condition read the param's entry value forever. `var i=lo;while(i\u003chi)` and `for (i in lo...hi)` spun infinitely (band-iteration = exactly the parallel-kernel pattern; `var i=0` worked). This is the documented \"n=n+1 in loop returns unmutated\" residual. Fix: identify params by SymbolKind::Parameter (new `is_parameter_symbol`), not register, at all 5 loop-phi sites (while/do-while/for). Test test_loop_counter_from_param.\n\nThe \"0xc11f trap-stub\" was NOT W0020 — it was a missing terminator. `finalize_lambda_terminator_static` (hir_to_mir.rs ~32716) added the implicit return to the lambda's ENTRY block only; for a body ending in a loop the entry block already has a terminator (branch into the loop), so finalize returned early, leaving the loop-EXIT block at its default `Unreachable` → `udf`/SIGILL on loop exit. Int closures escaped (trailing `return` terminated the exit block); plain Void FUNCTIONS escaped (ensure_terminator finalizes the current/exit block). Only **Void CLOSURES ending in a loop** trapped — exactly the parallelRows worker shape `(lo,hi,node)-\u003e{ var i=lo; while(i\u003chi){...;i++;} }`. Diagnosis: single-threaded repro TVD/TV1 (Void closure ending in band loop) traps on MAIN, disasm showed loop exit = `udf #0xc11f`; TVF (Void function) works, TVR (closure + explicit `return;`) works. Fix: finalize the block the builder ENDED on (loop-exit/merge), not entry. Test test_void_closure_trailing_loop.\n\nWorkerPool is now fully usable. (examples/concurrency/Main.hx still uses raw Thread.spawn for its 4 patterns; could be migrated to WorkerPool now that it works — optional follow-up.)\n\n- `new Atomic\u003cInt\u003e(0)` is INVALID — Atomic only has `Atomic.of(addr:Ptr\u003cT\u003e)` (no `new`). My early WP repros using `new Atomic` crashed on that, not WorkerPool.\n- WPd (construct only, never calls parallelRows) compiled fine because method bodies lower lazily/by-reachability — the compile hang (#3) only triggered when parallelRows was reached.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_workerpool_fix_chain` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}